      {
        "id": 80564,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-04T19:44:26.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'm a fan.</p><p>Thank you for simplifying effects that cross play area.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>This still leaves timing based triggers and effects to order the cards entered play, so only reaction triggers are affected by this rule.</p><p>As for Hairtrigger and Fowl we'll have to see if they redid the wording on Fowl cards.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>This is honestly how I've been playing the game. &nbsp;I don't think it makes it drastically easier, just more fun and a bit faster.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>As for static effects vs. static effects, they won't fall under this rule as they don't have timing. &nbsp;The new ones overwrite the old just like always, at least I would assume that is how it works.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:02:44.470Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
